  "equipment_type": "Submersible pump level controller",
  "applies_to": "Grundfos Level Control LC 2X2 controllers for submersible pump pits, fitted with a CIM 300 (BACnet MS/TP) or CIM 500 (BACnet IP) module.",
  "summary": "The LC 2X2 controls up to two submersible pumps from a level sensor or float switches. With a CIM 300 or CIM 500 module it exposes a fixed object list: pit level, energy, flow and water-quality readings, daily run-time counters, per-pump status inputs, an overall system status, writable level setpoints in centimetres and a multistate Auto/Forced start/Forced stop command per pump.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "CIM 300 V04.20.00 / CIM 500 V06.16 (as stated in the PICS)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object list from section 4.4 of the PICS (pages 24-26). Compared with the LC 2X1 it adds AV 2, BO 1, MI 2, AI 30-38 and BI 34-35, and drops the 16 user digital inputs (BI 18-33).",
    "AI 37/AI 38 (start counters today) are printed with unit 'min' and the same note as the run-time objects; listed as printed.",
    "The same object table is printed in the CIM 500 PICS (98690071, https://api.grundfos.com/literature/Grundfosliterature-6226722.pdf); CIM 300 gives BACnet MS/TP and CIM 500 BACnet IP.",
    "AI 39 bits 0-4 are warnings 1-5 and bits 8-12 alarms 1-5. AI 40 flags fitted sensors: bit 0 flow, 1 power/energy, 2-6 AI sensors 1-5, 7 turbidity, 8 pH, 9 conductivity, 10 pulse flow meter, 11 pressure, 12 level."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read the operating state (MI 0), pit level (AI 6) and the per-pump running and alarm inputs, and use MO 0/MO 1 to put each pump in Auto, Forced start or Forced stop. Alarms are reset with BO 0. The start, stop, high and dry-running levels can be written in centimetres through AO 0-4.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MO 0",
        "name": "Control Pump 1",
        "why": "Pump 1: 1 = Auto, 2 = Forced start, 3 = Forced stop"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 1",
        "name": "Control Pump 2",
        "why": "Pump 2: 1 = Auto, 2 = Forced start, 3 = Forced stop"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 0",
        "name": "Reset alarms",
        "why": "Alarm reset (1 = reset)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 0",
        "name": "System Operating Mode",
        "why": "Operating state: standby, pumping, alarm states..."
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 6",
        "name": "Pit water level",
        "why": "Pit level in cm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 8",
        "name": "Pump1Running",
        "why": "Pump 1 running status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 9",
        "name": "Pump2Running",
        "why": "Pump 2 running status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 12",
        "name": "Pump1Alarm",
        "why": "Pump 1 alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 13",
        "name": "Pump2Alarm",
        "why": "Pump 2 alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "Fault code",
        "why": "Active Grundfos fault code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "CIM 300 is a BACnet MS/TP master at 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800 baud; CIM 500 uses BACnet IP (Annex J).",
      "AV 0 lets the BMS set a custom device instance (0-0x3FFFFE).",
      "The CIM module fits inside the controller or in an external CIU box; the object list is the same either way.",
      "The PICS states that segmentation is not supported."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The level setpoints AO 0-4 are stored settings; write them only when they change, not cyclically.",
      "Pump 2 has a start-level object (AO 4) but no stop-level object in this table.",
      "AI 0/AI 1 are Grundfos fault and warning codes; decode them with the LC manual.",
      "BI 35 Control Status shows whether the controller is in auto or manual control."
    ]
  },
